# Billion Word Imputation — swarm solution (arcturus_kappa components)

Task: one interior word/token removed from each test sentence (location unknown).
Metric: mean character-level Levenshtein distance between submitted and original sentence (lower better).
Pipeline = **location model** (learned gap detector) + **fusion** with trigram LM signal + **word model** (RoBERTa-large MLM) + **expected-Levenshtein decision**.

## 1. Location: learned gap detector (`train_detector.py`, `infer_gapprobs.py`)
- Input: deleted sentence with a `[MASK]` slot inserted between **every** adjacent word pair.
- Encoder: `roberta-base` (HF, MIT license, general pretrained) — optionally initialised from a domain fine-tune.
- Heads: (a) gap head → softmax over all slots = `P(missing word before token k)`; (b) word head over top-30k whitespace words (training auxiliary).
- Training: one random interior token deleted per train sentence (train_v2.txt only), listwise CE over gaps + word CE; no test data used.
- One forward pass per sentence gives all-gap posteriors (cheap inference).
- Artifact: `detector_ft/ckpt_*.pt` (`encoder`, `gap_head`, `word_head`, `words`).

## 2. Location fusion (`fusion_lib.py`, `make_test_decisions.py`)
- Features per gap: detector gap prob/log/rank, detector top-word prob, trigram insertion `gain`/presence/rank (from antares_upsilon `TrigramLM`, counts on train_v2 only), gap-position fraction.
- Logistic regression (sklearn) fits `P(gap correct)` on the shared holdout (last 30k train lines, deleted with seed 20241031); features normalised. Trigrams for the holdout must be counted **excluding** those last 30k lines (contamination fix by antares_upsilon).
- Posterior = per-sentence softmax of the logistic scores; insert only when `max P(gap) >= tau` (tau tuned on holdout).

## 3. Word: RoBERTa-large MLM at the chosen gap (`word_at_oracle.py` helpers)
- `roberta-large` (HF, MIT license, general pretrained MLM; optionally fine-tuned on train_v2 by spica_psi) predicts the missing word given both sides.
- Insert a single `<mask>` at the chosen gap, take top-20 word-start candidates.
- Choose the inserted string minimising **expected character Levenshtein** over that top-k distribution (length penalty lambda; lambda=0.2).
- If posterior < tau → leave sentence unchanged (safe because a wrong-position insertion costs more than no insertion).

## 4. Reproduce
```
# detector training (GPU, train_v2 only)
python train_detector.py --init roberta-base --max_lines 2500000 --bs 160 --lr 1e-4
# detector gap posteriors
python infer_gapprobs.py --ckpt detector_ft/ckpt_XXXX.pt --input <sentences> --kind txt|csv --out det.pkl
# fusion + words + decisions
python make_test_decisions.py --hold_det ... --hold_tri ... --hold_meta ... --hold_orig ... \
    --test_det ... --test_tri ... --wl_ckpt roberta-large --out_decisions decisions.tsv --out_submission submission.csv
```

## External models (source logging)
| model | source | revision | license | purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| roberta-base | huggingface.co/roberta-base | main | MIT | detector encoder / base MLM |
| roberta-large | huggingface.co/roberta-large | main | MIT | word prediction (zero-shot / fine-tuned on train_v2) |
| (n-gram counts) | derived from data/train_v2.txt only | – | – | trigram insertion gain |

No competition labels, private data, or external solutions were used. Validation/holdout = last 30k lines of `data/train_v2.txt` (from the provided training data only).
